      "## How to Recreate the Effect at Home",
      "For a bedroom, living room, or reading nook, an [ultrasonic cool-mist diffuser](/product/autivara-4l-humidifying-diffuser) is the right tool for coverage — it's fully refillable with any compatible oil, so you're not locked into a proprietary cartridge system, and it disperses scent evenly rather than in short bursts. Run Tobacco Caramel or Noir Oud on a moderate, steady setting rather than a light intermittent one, which better matches the warm, present quality people describe about the in-store scent.",
      "[[cta]]Shop Home Diffusers|/home",
      "For the aesthetic side of things, the [Wood Grain Diffuser](/product/autivara-wood-grain-diffuser) fits this scent family especially well — its minimal, natural wood-toned design sits comfortably alongside the vintage rugs, rattan, and macrame that define the boho aesthetic this scent is built to complement, rather than looking out of place next to it.",
      "## Placing Your Diffuser for the Right Effect",
      "Retail stores run this kind of warm, incense-adjacent scent throughout the whole floor rather than concentrating it near the register, because the goal is an immersive, all-encompassing mood rather than a single accent note. At home, that translates to running your diffuser somewhere central — a living room or a bedroom you spend real time in — rather than a small, sealed closet where a warm, smoky scent can start to feel heavy in an enclosed space.",
      "If you want the scent to follow you outside the house, a [vent clip car diffuser](/product/autivara-magnetic-vent-diffuser) running the same Tobacco Caramel or Noir Oud oil keeps the mood consistent between your home and your commute, which matters if you're trying to build an actual signature scent rather than a one-room effect.",
      "[[cta]]Shop Car Diffusers|/auto",
      "## Frequently asked questions",
      "### Does Free People sell its in-store scent as a candle or spray?",
      "Not as a standard retail product. Free People has not released its exact in-store fragrance for sale, which is a large part of why 'what does Free People smell like' remains such a popular search online. The notes described here reflect what shoppers and scent communities consistently describe, not an official ingredient list.",
      "### Is Tobacco Caramel or Noir Oud an exact copy of Free People's scent?",
      "No, and no brand should claim an exact match to another retailer's proprietary in-store fragrance. Both are standalone Autivara scents built to capture the warm, earthy, incense-adjacent mood shoppers consistently describe — not a literal reproduction of a formula we don't have access to.",
      "### Should I choose Tobacco Caramel or Noir Oud?",
      "Tobacco Caramel leans warmer and slightly sweeter, closer to a cozy, worn-in feeling. Noir Oud leans smokier and more incense-like, closer to the boho market-stall side of the description. Try a small room first to see which matches your own memory of the store best.",
      "### How strong should I run the diffuser to match that boho, warm feeling?",
      "Moderate to steady rather than light. Unlike a clean, understated scent meant to fade into the background, this profile is meant to feel warm and present, so a light mist setting often won't produce the effect people are describing. Start moderate and adjust from there.",
      "### Can I use these scents in my car as well as at home?",
